Derek is a male name of English and Old German origin, possibly derived from Old German Theodoric [1], meaning power of the tribe or ruler of the people. Variants recently revived are Deryk, Deric and the Dutch form Dirk, popularised by the actor Dirk Bogarde In recent years it has been used occasionally as a family name, for example Bo Derek.

